--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
The array version of memset_two_targets_struct. The copy is a guarded store
to each possible target; where it is not taken, the old value is framed back.
For an array that field sensitivity splits into elements, that old value was
renamed as the bare whole-array symbol, whose version predates the store
`a->buf[1] = 'e'` (made to the element), so the framed-back element lost it.
Fails on a binary without the fix; stock CBMC 5.95 passes.
